     8	Python has emerged as one of the most popular programming languages, extensively utilized in domains such
     9	as machine learning, data analysis, and web applications. Python’s dynamic nature and extensive usage make
    10	it an attractive candidate for dynamic program analysis. However, unlike for other popular languages, there
    11	currently is no comprehensive benchmark suite of executable Python projects, which hinders the development
    12	of dynamic analyses. This work addresses this gap by presenting DyPyBench, the first benchmark of Python
    13	projects that is large-scale, diverse, ready-to-run (i.e., with fully configured and prepared test suites), and readyto-analyze (by integrating with the DynaPyt dynamic analysis framework). The benchmark encompasses 50
